<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/10/27/apple-imac-with-m6-lifestyle-261027-1793106250706-b5c135a4ea.jpg" alt="Source: Apple."><p class="image-caption">Source: Apple.</p></div>
<p id="p2">Apple’s daily hardware drops continued today with <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/10/apple-unveils-new-imac-with-m6/" rel="noopener noreferrer">a refresh to the iMac</a>. The new iMac upgrades from an M4 to an M6 chip, with the base model starting at $1,499 and available in blue, green, pink, yellow, purple, orange, and silver. There are two M6 configurations. The first has a 10-core CPU and a 10-core GPU, and the second has a 12-core CPU and a 12-core GPU, with the option of a nano-texture display. Memory starts at 16GB with a 24GB option for the 10-core iMac and an additional 32GB option for the 12-core model. All memory options feature 170GB/s bandwidth. Storage starts at 256GB and can be configured as high as 2TB on the 12-core model.</p>
<p id="p3">The new iMac also includes Wi-Fi 7, Bluetooth 6, and two or four Thunderbolt 4 ports depending on the model you choose. There is also an option for 2.5 Gigabit Ethernet on the 12-core iMac, up from 1 Gigabit on the M4 iMac. As in the past, the Magic Keyboard is color-matched with the iMac</p>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/10/27/apple-imac-with-m6-ports-261027-1793106257492-d2587eacad.jpg" alt="Source: Apple."><p class="image-caption">Source: Apple.</p></div>
<p id="p5">The display, which measures 23.5 inches diagonally, has a resolution of 4.5K with 500 nits of brightness and P3 wide color support. You can also connect up to two external 6K displays to the M6 iMac.</p>
<p id="p6">The new iMac also includes a 12MP Center Stage camera that supports Desk View for simulated top-down video, a pair of force-cancelling woofers, and two tweeters. Spatial Audio and Dolby Atmos audio are supported and a three-microphone array is built into the iMac, too.</p>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/10/27/apple-imac-with-m6-hero-261027-1793106244238-ab3e8272f7.jpg" alt="Source: Apple."><p class="image-caption">Source: Apple.</p></div>
<p id="p8"><a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/10/apple-unveils-new-imac-with-m6/" rel="noopener noreferrer">According to Apple</a>, the new iMac is 18x faster than Apple’s most popular Intel-based iMac, which is not surprising given how long it’s been since the introduction of Apple silicon. That said, I’m sure that a lot of households and businesses are still running those aging Intel iMacs and would benefit greatly from this update.</p>
<p id="p9"><a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/10/apple-unveils-new-imac-with-m6/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple also says</a> that the graphics performance is 3.3x better than an M1 iMac and 2x better than the most recent M4 model. On-device AI prompt processing in LM Studio is also 12x faster than the M1 iMac and 5x faster than the M4 model.</p>
<p id="p10">The M6 has already proven to be a very capable addition to Apple silicon and will undoubtedly make this the best iMac yet. It’s an excellent choice for anyone who wants an elegant, space-saving Mac and doesn’t need the horsepower of Apple’s pro line of Macs.</p>
<p id="p11">The M6 iMac <a href="https://www.apple.com/shop/buy-mac/imac" rel="noopener noreferrer">is available for preorder starting tomorrow</a> with deliveries beginning November 6.</p>
